Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:03.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Spiking Neural Networks promise low-power AI,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.79,0:00:08.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but training them over many timesteps is expensive in memory,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.24,0:00:11.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and running them repeats work at inference.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.38,0:00:14.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This ICML 2024 paper introduces T-RevSNN,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.38,0:00:20.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a Temporal Reversible architecture that turns off the temporal dynamics of most spiking
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.73,0:00:25.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}neurons and makes the few remaining temporal connections reversible.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.70,0:00:29.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The result is O(L) training memory and O(1) inference cost,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.01,0:00:37.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with state-of-the-art accuracy among CNN-based SNNs on ImageNet and up to 8.6 times better memory efficiency,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.97,0:00:42.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}2.0 times faster training, and 1.6 times lower inference energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.94,0:00:46.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Spiking Neural Networks are appealing because they promise brain-inspired,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.28,0:00:49.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}low-power computation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.62,0:00:52.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But to work well they are simulated over many timesteps,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.96,0:00:56.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and that comes at a steep cost.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.30,0:00:59.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}During training,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.64,0:01:02.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}memory grows with both the number of layers and the number of timesteps,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.98,0:01:06.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}on the order of L times T.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.32,0:01:09.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}At inference, repeating the input over T steps makes the energy scale with T as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.66,0:01:12.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The frustrating part is that current training methods can relieve one of these pressures
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.00,0:01:16.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but not the other at the same time,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.34,0:01:19.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}leaving SNNs stuck with a training memory and inference energy dilemma.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.98,0:01:23.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The key insight behind this work is surprisingly simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.03,0:01:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}When the authors examined the gradients that flow backward through time in a spiking network,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.08,0:01:32.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}they found that for most neurons those temporal gradients barely matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.13,0:01:36.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Only the neurons at a few key positions carry temporal information that is actually important.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.18,0:01:40.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}If that is true,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.23,0:01:44.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}then a natural question follows: why pay the full temporal cost for every neuron?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.29,0:01:48.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Prior methods either decouple training from the timestep to save memory,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.34,0:01:52.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}or shrink the number of inference steps to save energy,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.39,0:01:56.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but each one solves only half of the problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.44,0:02:00.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This paper asks whether both halves can be solved together.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.79,0:02:05.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Their answer is T-RevSNN, a Temporal Reversible architecture for spiking networks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.09,0:02:09.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The core idea is to turn off the temporal dynamics of most spiking neurons and keep them
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.40,0:02:13.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}on only at a few key positions,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.70,0:02:17.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}where the temporal connections are made reversible.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.00,0:02:22.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Reversibility means the network can recompute activations during the backward pass instead of storing them,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.30,0:02:26.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which brings training memory down to order L.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.61,0:02:30.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On top of that,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.91,0:02:35.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}they encode the input image only once and split both the features and the network into independent sub-networks,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.21,0:02:39.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so inference cost becomes constant, order one.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.51,0:02:43.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To make this sparse temporal design actually train well,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.82,0:02:48.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}they also redesign the basic SNN block in a ConvNeXt style and add a scaled residual connection.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.42,0:02:52.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Here is how it works in practice.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.12,0:02:55.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Instead of feeding the same image to the network at every timestep,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.82,0:02:59.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}T-RevSNN encodes the image just once, divides the encoded features into T groups,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.52,0:03:03.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and gives one group to each timestep.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.22,0:03:06.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The whole network is likewise split into T sub-networks that share parameters and exchange
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.92,0:03:10.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}temporal information only at the key,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.62,0:03:14.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}turned-on neurons.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.31,0:03:17.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Those key connections follow a multi-level temporal-reversible rule: the membrane potential
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.01,0:03:21.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}at one timestep can be exactly reconstructed from the next timestep's state and the incoming
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.71,0:03:25.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}spikes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.41,0:03:29.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Because the forward pass is reversible,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.11,0:03:32.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the backward pass only needs the membrane potentials of the final timestep,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.81,0:03:36.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so intermediate activations do not have to be stored.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.51,0:03:40.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}That is what collapses the training memory from order L times T down to order L.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.51,0:03:45.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The method is evaluated on both static and neuromorphic vision.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.44,0:03:50.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For static images they use ImageNet-1K at a resolution of 224 by 224.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.84,0:03:56.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For event-based data they use CIFAR10-DVS and the DVS128 Gesture dataset.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.55,0:04:01.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Crucially, they report not just accuracy but the real training cost,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.87,0:04:10.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}measuring peak GPU memory per image and per-epoch training time on six NVIDIA A100 GPUs under mixed precision.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.47,0:04:16.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}They compare against a broad set of baselines, including spiking ResNets,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.18,0:04:22.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}spiking Transformers, and other training-optimization methods such as OTTT, SLTT,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.52,0:04:25.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the spatially reversible S-RevSNN.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.79,0:04:28.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The results on ImageNet are strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.39,0:04:32.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}With about 30 million parameters and four timesteps,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.26,0:04:38.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}T-RevSNN reaches 73.2 percent top-1 accuracy while using only 85.7 megabytes of memory
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.66,0:04:42.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}per image and 2.8 millijoules of inference energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.38,0:04:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}That is the best accuracy among convolutional spiking ResNets,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.99,0:04:52.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it comes with the lowest training memory, the fastest training time,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.35,0:04:55.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the lowest inference energy in its class.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.70,0:05:00.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Compared against a leading spiking Transformer at similar accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.68,0:05:04.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}T-RevSNN uses 8.6 times less memory, trains 2 times faster,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.07,0:05:08.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and spends 1.6 times less inference energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.27,0:05:16.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A lighter 15 million parameter version still reaches nearly 70 percent accuracy at under 60 megabytes per image.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.90,0:05:21.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The ablations show that each design choice earns its place.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.10,0:05:27.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Simply applying temporal reversibility to a standard MS-ResNet-34 slashes training memory
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.43,0:05:33.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}from 267 down to 88 megabytes per image and cuts epoch time from 11.2 to 7.4 minutes,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.48,0:05:37.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}at the cost of only about one and a half accuracy points.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.54,0:05:44.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The multi-level temporal fusion between stages is worth roughly 1.2 points of accuracy on its own.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.51,0:05:48.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Varying the number of timesteps trades accuracy against cost,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.86,0:05:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the scaled residual connection helps the model converge noticeably faster,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.41,0:05:58.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reaching 60 percent accuracy in 25 epochs instead of 32.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.39,0:06:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors also confirm that temporal and spatial reversibility are orthogonal and can be stacked together.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.38,0:06:14.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To summarize the numbers that matter most: against a leading spiking Transformer at comparable accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.40,0:06:20.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}T-RevSNN delivers 8.6 times better memory efficiency, 2 times faster training,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.41,0:06:23.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and 1.6 times lower inference energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.26,0:06:27.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It reaches 73.2 percent top-1 accuracy on ImageNet-1K,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.42,0:06:33.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}using just 85.7 megabytes of memory per image and 2.8 millijoules per inference.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.59,0:06:40.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And it achieves all of this with order L training memory and order one inference cost.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.52,0:06:46.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The lasting message of this paper is that you do not need full temporal dynamics everywhere
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.11,0:06:48.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}to build a capable spiking network.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.26,0:06:51.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Because most temporal gradients turn out to be unimportant,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.89,0:06:57.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}switching off the temporal dynamics of most neurons and making the few remaining connections
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.54,0:07:02.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reversible gives you order L training memory and order one inference cost,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.09,0:07:03.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with almost no loss in accuracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.06,0:07:09.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}By removing the memory and training-time bottleneck that has held spiking networks back,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.46,0:07:12.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}T-RevSNN opens a path toward larger, more practical,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.66,0:07:15.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and more energy-efficient brain-inspired models.
